{"entryId":"1803","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1803:1","sourceSha256":"ffb7bdd9aed7a3ee23b649b6c85cfaee5607e91e17d5211c7f9823b3dc77792e","englishSha256":"2dc0113fab19300a82c67bb5da6b19ab96097e51627f5e6f1a216fc9c5adde10","citations":[{"id":"1803:1:link-01","he":[55,81],"en":[93,108],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Kallah_4.1"},"reference":"Tractate Kallah 4:1","assessment":"Kallah and its Yalkut parallel have Yochai bar Yoshiyah. Preserve Yochi in Heilprin’s gloss and the proposed Achi and Yoshiyahu as qualified variants.","evidence":[{"reference":"Tractate Kallah 4:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Kallah_4.1"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."},{"reference":"Yalkut Shimoni on Torah 786:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yalkut_Shimoni_on_Torah_786.7"},"witness":"Torat Emet"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[{"raw":"אולי צ\"ל אחי ובשס\"ח ר' יוחי בר יאשיהו","reason":"Kallah and Yalkut give Yochai in the compared text. Keep Heilprin’s Achi conjecture and the variant Yoshiyahu as reported.","evidence":[]}],"notes":[{"text":"The Kallah parallel reads Yochai bar Yoshiyah. Keep the different received gloss forms, the conjecture Achi, and the independently attested names of Yaakov and Shimon.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Midrash Tanchuma, Ki Tisa 4:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Midrash_Tanchuma%2C_Ki_Tisa_4.4"},"witness":"Midrash Tanchuma -- Torat Emet"},{"reference":"Shabbat 33b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_33b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Tractate Kallah 4:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tractate_Kallah_4.1"},"witness":"Talmud Bavli, Vilna 1883 ed."},{"reference":"Yalkut Shimoni on Torah 786:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yalkut_Shimoni_on_Torah_786.7"},"witness":"Torat Emet"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
